    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners`. The request is authorized, the DTO is bean-validated, and then everything is done imperatively inside `OwnerRegistrar.register(ownerFieldsDto, Idempotency-Key)` \u2014 there are **no** JPA lifecycle callbacks (`@PrePersist` etc.) and **no** Spring application events anywhere in the create path.\n\n## Validations (in the order they can reject the request)\n\n**Before `register` runs (in the controller layer):**\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` on `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` \u2192 403 if the caller isn't OWNER_ADMIN.\n2. **DTO Bean Validation** \u2014 `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` triggers all constraints: `firstName`/`lastName` `@NotNull @Pattern @Size(1..30)`; `city` `@NotNull @Pattern @Size(1..80)`; `telephone` `@NotNull @Size(1..20)`; `email` `@Email @Size`; `address`/`addressLine1` non-blank `@Size`; `addressLine2 @Size(max 255)`; `postcode @Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`; `@Valid` on `registrationDate`/`birthDate`. Failure \u2192 400 (via `ExceptionControllerAdvice`). *(The entity-level constraints on `Owner`/`Person` are **not** enforced on this path \u2014 `saveOwner` calls `save` without `@Valid`.)*\n\n**Inside `register` (each throws `OwnerRegistrationException` with the status shown):**\n3. **Future registration date** \u2014 after defaulting null \u2192 `today`, reject if after today \u2192 400.\n4. **Daily create quota** \u2014 counts existing owners on the (business-day-adjusted) registration date; `>= 100` \u2192 429.\n5. **Address present** \u2014 after normalization/merge of `addressLine1/2` vs `address`, null result \u2192 400.\n6. **Telephone normalizable** \u2014 `TelephoneNormalizer.normalize` (E.164, assumes +61); null \u2192 400.\n7. **Telephone national-number length** \u2014 e.g. +61 \u2192 9 digits, +1 \u2192 10; invalid \u2192 400.\n8. **Email syntax** \u2014 if present, must match `EMAIL_PATTERN` \u2192 400.\n9. **Email not disposable** \u2014 rejects mailinator.com / tempmail.com / guerrillamail.com \u2192 400.\n10. **Postcode** \u2014 if present, `^[0-9]{4}$` **and** valid-for-city range (NSW 2000\u20132099 / VIC 3000\u20133099 / QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown city passes) \u2192 400.\n11. **Duplicate identity** \u2014 SHA-256 identity key over `telephone | lowercased email | soundex(lastName)` compared to every non-deleted owner; collision \u2192 409.\n12. **Per-city capacity** \u2014 owners in the same normalized city `>= 50` \u2192 409.\n\n## Side-effects (on a successful create, in order)\n\nBefore persistence, `register` **mutates the owner** through these steps:\n1. **Idempotency replay check** \u2014 if the `Idempotency-Key` header was seen before, returns the original owner (200, no new create) instead of continuing.\n2. Default `registrationDate` to `today` if null.\n3. **Business-day roll-forward** \u2014 advances the date past weekends and the fixed 2026 public-holiday set.\n4. **Address normalization** \u2014 trim/collapse/upper-case, expand ST/RD/AVE, prefer structured lines; writes back.\n5. **Telephone canonicalization** \u2014 stores the normalized E.164 value.\n6. **Email canonicalization** \u2014 trims and lower-cases; stores.\n7. **Household id** \u2014 first 12 hex of `SHA-256(\"V2|\"+lastName+\"|\"+postcode)`.\n8. **`capacityWarning`** flag set when city count is in 40\u201349.\n9. **Member id** \u2014 `<region><fiscalYear><hash8><Luhn check>`, de-duplicated against existing member ids (`-n` suffix).\n10. **`namesakeCount`** \u2014 count of existing owners with the same first+last name.\n11. **`bulkSignupWarning`** \u2014 set when that day's created count > 80.\n12. **`possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf`** \u2014 soft-match (same last-name soundex + postcode, different identity key) \u2192 lowest matching id.\n\nThen:\n13. **DB insert** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner` \u2192 `ownerRepository.save` (the only write; assigns the generated id).\n14. **Idempotency store** \u2014 records `idempotencyKey \u2192 owner.id` in the in-memory `ConcurrentHashMap`.\n15. **Audit log** \u2014 `OwnerAuditor.ownerCreated` emits two `AUDIT`-logger lines (human + JSON with a monotonic sequence number).\n16. **Welcome notification** \u2014 `WelcomeNotifier.welcome` emits a `NOTIFY`-logger line.\n17. **Response** \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto` (deriving many read-only fields, some issuing further `findAllOwners()` reads) and returns **201 Created** with a `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header.\n\nA couple of things worth flagging: the pipeline is **not** wrapped in a single transaction (each `ClinicService` method opens its own), and it calls `findAllOwners()` repeatedly (quota, duplicate, city count, member-id, namesake, plus again during response mapping), so a create is many full-table scans rather than one atomic unit."
